# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Cast Pacifism, attach it to an opposing creature, then remove that creature so the Aura is cleaned up.
# Forcing: Four untapped lands pay for Pacifism and Lightning Bolt; one opposing Grizzly Bears is the only legal Aura target and removal target.
# AI behavior: The opponent has no hand and one creature, so the scripted human line has no opponent decisions before the assertions.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN   = Pacifism resolves attached, then both the creature and illegal Aura reach their owner's graveyards.
#   LOSE  = target selection, Aura attachment, Bolt removal, or state-based cleanup is missing.
#   TIMEOUT = a cast, target prompt, resolution, or cleanup horizon does not complete.
# Card roles:
#   Pacifism — representative Enchant Aura; its static effect makes the attachment meaningful.
#   Lightning Bolt — deterministic post-attachment creature removal.
#   Grizzly Bears — one legal opposing creature target and removal target.
#   Plains/Mountain — deterministic mana for both spells.
# Protocol path: Cast, SelectTargetsReq, PlayerSelectingTargets, PlayerSubmittedTargets, TargetSpec, ResolutionStart/Complete, AttachmentCreated, persistent Attachment, ZoneTransfer, and Aura SBA cleanup.

[metadata]
